Hi Avery,

Teams that replace one recurring meeting a week with a Loom save about 40 hours per person per year. Here are five places to start:

1. Weekly team update: record once, everyone watches at 1.5x
2. Product walkthroughs for sales: one recording, reused on every call
3. Code review context: talk through the PR instead of typing a novel
4. Customer onboarding: a personal welcome that scales
5. Bug reports: show, don't describe

New in Loom: AI-generated titles, chapters and summaries on every recording, and a "watch later" queue.

